Decision 66 argues the throw "closes one real hole": *"a task id with no alphanumeric character at all slugs to the empty string, which would make `compiledDir` the shared `<store>/sessions/compiled`."*

This is inaccurate against `sessionSlug` in [`src/core/session-lifecycle.service.ts`](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/228ec3455689c38e83755890fb9aa4c5978c58e4/src/core/session-lifecycle.service.ts#L51-L54):
```ts
function sessionSlug(taskId: string, existing: number): string {
  const stem = taskId.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]+/g, '-').slice(0, 24);
  return existing === 0 ? stem : `${stem}-${existing}`;
}
```
`[^a-zA-Z0-9]+` is a **run** of non-alphanumeric characters replaced by a **single** `-`. So a task id with zero alphanumeric characters (e.g. `"!!!"`, `"---"`, a lone space) slugs to `"-"`, not `""` — and `"-"` passes `SESSION_ID_PATTERN` fine, so it doesn't trigger the collision the doc describes at all. Only a task id that is *itself already the empty string* produces an empty stem (since `.replace()` is a no-op on `""`).

The stated trigger condition is strictly broader than, and distinct from, the real one. A reader auditing whether this fix's edge-case coverage is complete would be misled about what input actually produces the described collision. Since `docs/09-decisions.md` is this repo's authoritative record (it "wins over 00-08 where they conflict" per AGENTS.md), the technical claim it makes about its own fix should be correct.

